[133.364306, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@595343f7d16a:/app# "]
[140.828452, "i", "cat << 'EOF' > /app/vuln-report.md\n# Vulnerability-Driven Entry Analysis Report\n\n## Summary\nAn investigation into potential software vulnerabilities (CVEs) as entry vectors was conducted. Based on system logs, scanner results, and threat intelligence, **no software vulnerability (CVE) was exploited** to gain entry to `redis-prod-01`. The initial access was purely driven by application misconfiguration.\n\n---\n\n## Vulnerability Assessment & Findings\n\n### 1. Automated Vulnerability Scan Results\n- **Scanner Feed**: The security scanner output file `/sas/vulns.json:1` returned an empty list `[]` (`/sas/vulns.json:1`).\n- **Finding**: No unpatched CVEs were flagged or detected on the target host by vulnerability scanning components.\n\n### 2. Reconciliation of Stale Ticket Claims (BlueKeep False Lead)\n- **Draft Change Ticket Claim**: Row 2 of `/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md:10` proposed patching `CVE-2019-0708 (BlueKeep)` on `RDP` (`/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md:10`).\n- **Forensic Assessment**: **INVALID / INCORRECT**.\n  - `CVE-2019-0708` (BlueKeep) is a Remote Code Execution vulnerability in Microsoft Windows Remote Desktop Services (RDP).\n  - The target system `redis-prod-01` is running Linux Debian 12 (`/disk/etc/os-release:1`), and no RDP services are installed or exposed (`/disk/etc/passwd:1`).\n  - Threat Intelligence confirms the entry vector was unauthenticated Redis access (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:12`).\n\n### 3. Actual Entry Vector: Application Misconfiguration\n- Rather than a software vulnerability exploit, initial access was facilitated by severe administrative misconfiguration of the Redis service:\n  - **Protected Mode Disabled**: `protected-mode no` (`/disk/etc/redis/redis.conf:3`).\n  - **Unrestricted Binding**: `bind 0.0.0.0` (`/disk/etc/redis/redis.conf:3`).\n  - **No Authentication**: `no password set` (`/disk/etc/redis/redis.conf:3`).\n- This configuration allowed remote unauthenticated clients to connect directly and issue administrative Redis commands, including `CONFIG SET` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:13`).\n\n---\n\n## Conclusion & Confidence Statement\n- **Confidence Level**: **HIGH**.\n- **Entry Vector Classification**: Misconfiguration / Weak Authentication (ATT&CK T1133) rather than Vulnerability Exploitation (ATT&CK T1190).\nEOF\n"]
[140.828823, "o", "cat << 'EOF' > /app/vuln-report.md\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[140.828862, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[140.829391, "o", "# Vulnerability-Driven Entry Analysis Report\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ## Summary\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[140.831166, "o", "An investigation into potential software vulnerabilities (CVEs) as entry vectors was conducted. Based on system logs, scanner results, and threat intelligence, **no software vulnerability (CVE) was exploited** to gain entry to `redis-prod-01`. The initial access was purely driven by application misconfiguration.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ---\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ## Vulnerability Assessment & Findings\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ### 1. Automated Vulnerability Scan Results\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - **Scanner Feed**: The security scanner output file `/sas/vulns.json:1` returned an empty list `[]` (`/sas/vulns.json:1`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - **Finding**: No unpatched CVEs were flagged or detected on the target host by vulnerability scanning components.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ### 2. Reconciliation of Stale Ticket Claims (BlueKeep False Lead)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - **Draft Change Ticket Claim**: Row 2 of `/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md:10` proposed patching `CVE-2019-0708 (BlueKeep)` on `RDP` (`/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md:10`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - **Forensic Assessment**: **INVALID / INCORRECT**.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   - `CVE-2019-0708` (BlueKeep) is a Remote Code Execution vulnerability in Microsoft Windows Remote Desktop Services (RDP).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   - The target system `redis-prod-01` is running Linux Debian 12 (`/disk/etc/os-release:1`), and no RDP services are installed or exposed (`/disk/etc/passwd:1`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   - Threat Intelligence confirms the entry vector was unauthenticated Redis access (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:12`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ### 3. Actual Entry Vector: Application Misconfiguration\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - Rather than a software vulnerability exploit, initial access was facilitated by severe administrative misconfiguration of the Redis service:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   - **Protected Mode Disabled**: `protected-mode no` (`/disk/etc/redis/redis.conf:3`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   - **Unrestricted Binding**: `bind 0.0.0.0` (`/disk/etc/redis/redis.conf:3`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   - **No Authentication**: `no password set` (`/disk/etc/redis/redis.conf:3`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - This configuration allowed remote unauthenticated clients to connect directly and issue administrative Redis commands, including `CONFIG SET` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:13`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ---\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ## Conclusion & Confidence Statement\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - **Confidence Level**: **HIGH**.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - **Entry Vector Classification**: Misconfiguration / Weak Authentication (ATT&CK T1133) rather than Vulnerability Exploitation (ATT&CK T1190).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> EOF\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[140.83203, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@595343f7d16a:/app# "]
[148.537064, "i", "cat << 'EOF' > /app/baseline-report.md\n# Baseline Configuration Assessment Report\n\n## Executive Summary\nA security baseline evaluation was performed against host `redis-prod-01` by inspecting `/sas/baseline.json:1` and system configuration files under `/disk/etc/`. Critical baseline controls failed, directly enabling unauthenticated remote code execution and persistent compromise.\n\n---\n\n## Baseline Audit & Findings\n\n### Check CHK-05: Redis Configuration Baseline (`BAS-01`)\n- **Target File**: `/etc/redis/redis.conf` (`/sas/baseline.json:2`, `/sas/alerts.json:18`).\n- **Status**: **FAILED / CRITICAL**.\n- **Observed Configuration**: `/disk/etc/redis/redis.conf:3` contains:\n  ```text\n  Redis protected-mode no; bind 0.0.0.0; no password set\n  ```\n- **Deficiencies Identified**:\n  1. **Unrestricted Network Binding (`bind 0.0.0.0`)**: Listens on all IPv4 interfaces rather than loopback (`127.0.0.1`) or a dedicated private internal management network.\n  2. **Protected Mode Disabled (`protected-mode no`)**: Disables built-in protection that restricts queries from non-loopback interfaces when no password is set.\n  3. **Missing Authentication (`no password set`)**: Omits `requirepass` authentication directive, granting full administrative control to any network client.\n  4. **Dangerous Command Availability**: High-risk Redis commands (`CONFIG`, `SAVE`, `MODULE`, `EVAL`) were not renamed or disabled.\n\n---\n\n## Secondary System Baseline Weaknesses\n\n### 1. Dynamic Linker Preload Controls (`/etc/ld.so.preload`)\n- **Status**: **FAILED**.\n- **Evidence**: `/disk/etc/ld.so.preload:1` contains an unmonitored pre-load entry pointing to `/lib/.hide.so` (`/disk/etc/ld.so.preload:1`).\n- **Deficiency**: Absence of file integrity monitoring (FIM) or write restriction on `/etc/ld.so.preload` enabled silent dynamic linker hijacking.\n\n### 2. Temp Directory Execution Permissions (`/tmp`)\n- **Status**: **FAILED**.\n- **Evidence**: Executable binaries were staged and executed directly from `/tmp/.redis/` (`/disk/tmp/.redis/kdevtmpfsi`, `/disk/tmp/.redis/exp.so`).\n- **Deficiency**: Mount options for `/tmp` omitted `noexec`, allowing untrusted binaries to run.\n\n--- \n\n## Required Baseline Hardening Baseline Specifications\n1. Enforce `bind 127.0.0.1` or internal IP in `/etc/redis/redis.conf` (`/disk/etc/redis/redis.conf:3`).\n2. Enforce `protected-mode yes` in `/etc/redis/redis.conf` (`/disk/etc/redis/redis.conf:3`).\n3. Set strong authentication via `requirepass <complex_password>` in `/etc/redis/redis.conf` (`/disk/etc/redis/redis.conf:3`).\n4. Rename or disable dangerous Redis commands (`rename-command CONFIG \"\"`).\n5. Implement FIM alerts on `/etc/ld.so.preload` (`/disk/etc/ld.so.preload:1`) and crontabs (`/disk/var/spool/cron/crontabs/root:5`).\nEOF\n"]
[148.539975, "o", "cat << 'EOF' > /app/baseline-report.md\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[148.540004, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> # Baseline Configuration Assessment Report\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ## Executive Summary\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> A security baseline evaluation was performed against host `redis-prod-01` by inspecting `/sas/baseline.json:1` and system configuration files under `/disk/etc/`. Critical baseline controls failed, directly enabling unauthenticated remote code execution and persistent compromise.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ---\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ## Baseline Audit & Findings\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ### Check CHK-05: Redis Configuration Baseline (`BAS-01`)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - **Target File**: `/etc/redis/redis.conf` (`/sas/baseline.json:2`, `/sas/alerts.json:18`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - **Status**: **FAILED / CRITICAL**.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - **Observed Configuration**: `/disk/etc/redis/redis.conf:3` contains:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   ```text\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   Redis protected-mode no; bind 0.0.0.0; no password set\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   ```\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - **Deficiencies Identified**:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   1. **Unrestricted Network Binding (`bind 0.0.0.0`)**: Listens on all IPv4 interfaces rather than loopback (`127.0.0.1`) or a dedicated private internal management network.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   2. **Protected Mode Disabled (`protected-mode no`)**: Disables built-in protection that restricts queries from non-loopback interfaces when no password is set.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   3. **Missing Authentication (`no password set`)**: Omits `requirepass` authentication directive, granting full administrative control to any network client. \r\u001bM\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u00