restriction on `/etc/ld.so.preload` enabled silent dynamic linker hijacking.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ### 2. Temp Directory Execution Permissions (`/tmp`)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - **Status**: **FAILED**.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - **Evidence**: Executable binaries were staged and executed directly from `/tmp/.redis/` (`/disk/tmp/.redis/kdevtmpfsi`, `/disk/tmp/.redis/exp.so`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - **Deficiency**: Mount options for `/tmp` omitted `noexec`, allowing untrusted binaries to run.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> --- \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ## Required Baseline Hardening Baseline Specifications\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
