[169.121428, "i", "cat << 'EOF' > /app/remediation-plan.md\n# Prioritised Remediation Plan & Reconciled Change Ticket CHG-5677\n\n## Reconciled Change Ticket (CHG-5677)\n\n| # | Action | Target | Status | Note / Evidence Citation |\n|---|--------|--------|--------|--------------------------|\n| 1 | Block source IP inbound | `198.51.100.170` | proposed | **CORRECTED**: Replaced stale IP `203.0.113.9` with verified attacker C2 IP `198.51.100.170` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:5`, `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1`). |\n| 2 | Harden Redis Configuration & Auth | `/etc/redis/redis.conf` | proposed | **REPLACED**: Removed irrelevant BlueKeep CVE-2019-0708 (`/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md:10`). Hardening Redis with `protected-mode yes`, `bind 127.0.0.1`, and `requirepass` (`/disk/etc/redis/redis.conf:3`). |\n| 3 | Remove & Quarantine Cron Persistence | `/var/spool/cron/crontabs/root` | OPEN | **DOWNGRADED**: Changed status from unverified `DONE` (`/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md:11`) to `OPEN`. Backup/quarantine cron file containing malicious beacon (`/disk/var/spool/cron/crontabs/root:5`, `/sas/alerts.json:10`). |\n| 4 | Remove Dynamic Linker Preload Hijack | `/etc/ld.so.preload` | TODO | **ADDED (SILENT)**: Backup/quarantine `/etc/ld.so.preload` referencing `/lib/.hide.so` (`/disk/etc/ld.so.preload:1`). |\n| 5 | Quarantine Staged Binary Artifacts | `/tmp/.redis/` | TODO | **ADDED (SILENT)**: Stop miner process PID 1337 (`/sas/alerts.json:2`) and move `/tmp/.redis/kdevtmpfsi` (`/disk/tmp/.redis/kdevtmpfsi`) and `/tmp/.redis/exp.so` (`/disk/tmp/.redis/exp.so`) to secure quarantine directory. |\n| 6 | Quarantine Anti-Forensic Cache Fragment | `/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin` | TODO | **ADDED (SILENT)**: Securely quarantine `/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin` (`/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1`). |\n\n---\n\n## Phase-by-Phase Remediation Execution Plan\n\n> **Rule**: All steps prioritize backup/quarantine over direct deletion to preserve evidence for post-incident forensic validation.\n\n### Phase 1: Immediate Network & Process Containment\n1. **Block Attacker IP at Firewall**:\n   ```bash\n   # Block inbound and outbound communication with attacker C2 IP (/sas/cti/advisory.txt:5)\n   iptables -A INPUT -s 198.51.100.170 -j DROP\n   iptables -A OUTPUT -d 198.51.100.170 -j DROP\n   ```\n   *Citation*: `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:5`, `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1`\n\n2. **Isolate & Stop Mining Process**:\n   ```bash\n   # Terminate active miner process PID 1337 or matching executable name (/sas/alerts.json:2)\n   pkill -f kdevtmpfsi || kill -9 1337\n   ```\n   *Citation*: `/sas/alerts.json:2`, `/disk/tmp/.redis/kdevtmpfsi`\n\n3. **Isolate Redis Network Exposure**:\n   ```bash\n   # Temporarily stop Redis service during remediation\n   systemctl stop redis-server\n   ```\n   *Citation*: `/disk/etc/redis/redis.conf:3`\n\n---\n\n### Phase 2: Evidence Preservation & Quarantine\n1. **Create Secure Quarantine Storage**:\n   ```bash\n   mkdir -m 700 /var/quarantine_evidence\n   ```\n\n2. **Quarantine Persistence Mechanisms (Cron & LD_PRELOAD)**:\n   ```bash\n   # Backup/Quarantine root crontab (/disk/var/spool/cron/crontabs/root:5)\n   cp -a /var/spool/cron/crontabs/root /var/quarantine_evidence/root_crontab.bak\n   crontab -r -u root\n\n   # Backup/Quarantine LD_PRELOAD file (/disk/etc/ld.so.preload:1)\n   mv /etc/ld.so.preload /var/quarantine_evidence/ld.so.preload.bak\n   if [ -f /lib/.hide.so ]; then\n     mv /lib/.hide.so /var/quarantine_evidence/hide.so.bak\n   fi\n   ```\n   *Citations*: `/disk/var/spool/cron/crontabs/root:5`, `/disk/etc/ld.so.preload:1`\n\n3. **Quarantine Staged Binaries & Cache Files**:\n   ```bash\n   # Quarantine /tmp/.redis contents (/disk/tmp/.redis/kdevtmpfsi, /disk/tmp/.redis/exp.so)\n   mv /tmp/.redis /var/quarantine_evidence/tmp_redis_bak\n\n   # Quarantine wiped cache fragment (/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1)\n   mv /var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin /var/quarantine_evidence/wiped.bin.bak\n   ```\n   *Citations*: `/disk/tmp/.redis/kdevtmpfsi`, `/disk/tmp/.redis/exp.so`, `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1`\n\n---\n\n### Phase 3: Service Hardening & Eradication\n1. **Secure Redis Configuration** (`/etc/redis/redis.conf`):\n "]
[169.121459, "i", "  Update `/etc/redis/redis.conf` to enforce the following security parameters:\n   ```text\n   bind 127.0.0.1\n   protected-mode yes\n   requirepass <STRONG_GENERATED_PASSWORD>\n   rename-command CONFIG \"\"\n   rename-command MODULE \"\"\n   rename-command EVAL \"\"\n   ```\n   *Citation*: `/disk/etc/redis/redis.conf:3`, `/sas/baseline.json:2`\n\n2. **Restart & Validate Redis**:\n   ```bash\n   systemctl restart redis-server\n   systemctl status redis-server\n   ```\n\n---\n\n## Post-Remediation Verification Plan\n\n1. **Verify Network Exposure**:\n   ```bash\n   # Ensure Redis port 6379 is bound exclusively to 127.0.0.1\n   ss -tlpn | grep 6379\n   ```\n\n2. **Verify Process Integrity**:\n   ```bash\n   # Ensure no unexpected processes running from /tmp or consuming high CPU\n   ps aux | grep -E 'kdevtmpfsi|xmrig|tmp'\n   ```\n\n3. **Verify Preload Security**:\n   ```bash\n   # Ensure /etc/ld.so.preload does not exist\n   ls -la /etc/ld.so.preload\n   ```\n\n4. **Verify Cron Integrity**:\n   ```bash\n   # Inspect current cron entries\n   crontab -l -u root\n   ```\nEOF\n"]
